{"name":"Blackberry Tart","hex":"#563342","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blackberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fruit-bearing shrub of the aggregate species Rubus fruticosus and some hybrids.","The soft fruit borne by this shrub, formed of a black (when ripe) cluster of drupelets."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To gather or forage for blackberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackberry"},{"term":"tart","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sharp to the taste; acid; sour.","High or too high in acidity."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of small open pie, or piece of pastry, now typically containing jelly (US) / jam (UK) or conserve, or sometimes other fillings (chocolate, custard, egg, butter, historically even meat or other savory fillings).","A melt (block of wax for use in a tart burner)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tart"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blackberry","blocks":[{"text":"A blackberry is an edible fruit produced by many species in the genus Rubus in the family Rosaceae, hybrids among these species within the subgenus Rubus, and hybrids between the subgenera Rubus and Idaeobatus. The taxonomy of blackberries has historically been confused because of hybridization and apomixis so that species have often been grouped together and called species aggregates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Ripe%2C_ripening%2C_and_green_blackberries.jpg/330px-Ripe%2C_ripening%2C_and_green_blackberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blackberry","wikidata":"Q19842373"},{"title":"Tart","blocks":[{"text":"A tart is a baked dish consisting of a filling over a pastry base with an open top not covered with pastry. The pastry is usually shortcrust pastry; the filling may be sweet or savoury, though modern tarts are usually fruit-based, sometimes with custard. Tartlet refers to a miniature tart; an example would be egg tarts. The categories of \"tart\", \"flan\", and \"pie\" overlap, with no sharp distinctions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Raspberry_tart.jpg/330px-Raspberry_tart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tart","wikidata":"Q1142483"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG/500px-Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG/1280px-Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG/500px-Rubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARubus_fruticosus_Luc_Viatour.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg/250px-Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg/500px-Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg/250px-Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHalved_blackberry_(Rubus_fruticosus).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Raspberry_-_hal